Project Testing Phase
Legalease – Project Testing Phase

The Project Testing Phase is the stage where the completed Legalease system is checked to ensure that all features work correctly, securely, and according to the project requirements.

1. Objective

The main objectives of testing are:

Verify that all modules work correctly.
Identify and fix errors and bugs.
Check the accuracy and relevance of system responses.
Test database operations.
Verify security and user authentication.
Check the usability and performance of the application.
Ensure that the system meets the planned requirements.
2. Testing Process

The testing process follows these steps:

Developed System
       ↓
Test Planning
       ↓
Unit Testing
       ↓
Integration Testing
       ↓
Functional Testing
       ↓
Security Testing
       ↓
Usability Testing
       ↓
Performance Testing
       ↓
Bug Fixing
       ↓
Final Validation
3. Types of Testing
A. Unit Testing

Individual modules are tested separately.

Examples:

Login module
Search module
AI assistant
Document generator
Database functions

Purpose: To ensure that each individual component works correctly.

B. Integration Testing

Different modules are tested together.

For example:

User Question
     ↓
Frontend
     ↓
Backend
     ↓
AI Module
     ↓
Database
     ↓
Response
     ↓
Frontend

This verifies that information flows correctly between different parts of the system.

C. Functional Testing

Functional testing checks whether the application performs the functions specified in the requirements.

Test	Expected Result
Register with valid details	Account created
Login with valid credentials	Dashboard displayed
Login with invalid credentials	Error message displayed
Search legal topic	Relevant information displayed
Submit legal question	Appropriate general response displayed
Select document template	Template opened
Enter valid document details	Document generated
Open resource	Appropriate official resource displayed
D. AI Response Testing

Since Legalease uses an AI-assisted legal-information feature, different types of questions should be tested.

Examples:

Consumer-related questions
Employment-related questions
Property-related questions
Cybercrime-related questions
General legal-information questions
Ambiguous questions
Questions outside the system's supported scope

The responses should be checked for relevance, clarity, source grounding, and appropriate limitations.

E. Database Testing

Database testing verifies:

Data insertion
Data retrieval
Data updating
Data deletion
User-query history
Data consistency
Database security
F. Security Testing

Security testing checks:

Login authentication
Password protection
Authorization
Input validation
Session management
Unauthorized access
Protection of user information
G. Usability Testing

The application is tested from a user's perspective.

The following are evaluated:

Ease of navigation
Readability
Button placement
Mobile responsiveness
Clarity of instructions
Ease of asking questions
Ease of generating documents
H. Performance Testing

The system is checked for:

Response time
Page-loading speed
Database performance
AI response time
Multiple-user handling
